<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n115102" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῡμ-ός</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χέω</span>) used much <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				like
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χυλός</span>
			, though sts. distd. fr. it (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χυλός</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b>
			<i>juice</i> of plants, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				6.6.3
			</span></i> (cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				17
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>).<i><span class="en">
				327
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				60a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				60b
			</span></i>(pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				554a13
			</span></i>(pl.), <i><span class="en">
				596b17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.1.1
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>animal juices,</i> 'humours', <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>VM</u>
				18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				556b22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PA</u>
				676a16
			</span></i>; <i>juice</i> in a wider sense covering <i><span class="en">
				1.1
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				380b2
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				32
			</span></i>: freq. in later writers, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				15.62
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				16.497
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				2.45
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμίπεπτοι χ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					6.258
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέψαι τοὺς χ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				253
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χυμός: σίελος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ τῶν χυμῶν κενώσεις</span>
			include <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτύσματα</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				16.644
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>flavour,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅμα τῇ γεύσει ὁ χ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					245a9
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Mete.</u>
				356a13
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>de An.</u>
				414b11
			</span></i>: but not of the <i>action of causing taste,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ τοῦ χ. [ἐνέργεια] ἀνώνυμος</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				426a15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰχθῦν . . , ἔχοντα τοὺς χ. ἐν αὑτῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arched.
					2.9
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀσμαί, χρόαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.646b
			</span></i> (and so interchangeable with 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χυλός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			 (q.v.), <i><span class="en">
				Diocl.Fr.
				138
			</span></i>): several varieties distd. by <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				6.4.1
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.913b
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
